sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User
    participant API
    participant EventSvc as Event Service
    participant BookingSvc as Booking Service
    participant Redis
    participant PostgreSQL as PostgreSQL<br/>(Transaction)
    participant LotterySvc as Lottery Service

    Note over User,LotterySvc: Phase 1: Event Creation (Admin)
    User->>+API: POST /events (admin auth)
    API->>+EventSvc: Create(title, capacity, winner_count, draw_at)
    EventSvc->>+PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO events<br/>status='open'
    PostgreSQL-->>-EventSvc: event_id
    EventSvc-->>-API: Event created
    API-->>-User: 201 Created

    Note over User,LotterySvc: Phase 2: Ticket Booking (Authenticated User)
    User->>+API: POST /events/{id}/book
    API->>+BookingSvc: BookWithLock(event_id, user_id)
    
    BookingSvc->>BookingSvc: Enter in-process per-event FIFO queue<br/>(waits in arrival order, no DB connection held)

    BookingSvc->>+Redis: SET NX lock:booking:event:{id}<br/>token=random_hex, TTL=LOCK_TTL<br/>(retried with bounded jittered backoff)
    alt Lock Acquired within LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT (default 10s)
        Redis-->>BookingSvc: OK (lock acquired)

        BookingSvc->>+PostgreSQL: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        PostgreSQL-->>BookingSvc: tx started

        BookingSvc->>PostgreSQL: SELECT status, capacity<br/>FROM events WHERE id=?<br/>FOR UPDATE
        PostgreSQL-->>BookingSvc: status='open', capacity=10

        alt User already booked (checked first)
            BookingSvc-->>API: ErrAlreadyBooked
            API-->>User: 409 already_booked
        end

        alt Status is NOT 'open'
            BookingSvc-->>API: ErrEventNotOpen
            API-->>User: 409 event_not_open
        end

        BookingSvc->>PostgreSQL: SELECT COUNT(*)<br/>FROM bookings WHERE event_id=?
        PostgreSQL-->>BookingSvc: count=8

        alt Count >= Capacity
            BookingSvc-->>API: ErrEventFull
            API-->>User: 409 event_full
        end
        
        BookingSvc->>PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO bookings<br/>(event_id, user_id)
        PostgreSQL-->>BookingSvc: booking created
        
        BookingSvc->>PostgreSQL: COMMIT
        PostgreSQL-->>-BookingSvc: committed
        
        BookingSvc->>Redis: Lua compare-and-delete lock<br/>(owner-safe release, then next queued request runs)
        Redis-->>-BookingSvc: lock released

        BookingSvc-->>-API: Booking confirmed
        API-->>-User: 201 Created

    else Wait exceeded LOCK_WAIT_TIMEOUT
        Redis-->>BookingSvc: still held after bounded retries
        BookingSvc-->>-API: ErrEventBusy (retryable)
        API-->>-User: 503 event_busy + Retry-After
    end

    Note over BookingSvc,Redis: If Redis is unreachable the booking fails closed with 500:<br/>no overselling, but bookings are unavailable until Redis recovers

    Note over User,LotterySvc: Phase 3: Close Event (Admin)
    User->>+API: PUT /events/{id}/close
    API->>+EventSvc: Close(event_id)
    EventSvc->>+PostgreSQL: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    EventSvc->>PostgreSQL: SELECT status FROM events<br/>WHERE id=? FOR UPDATE
    PostgreSQL-->>EventSvc: status='open'
    EventSvc->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE events<br/>SET status='closed'<br/>WHERE id=?
    EventSvc->>PostgreSQL: COMMIT
    PostgreSQL-->>-EventSvc: committed
    EventSvc-->>-API: Event closed
    API-->>-User: 200 OK

    Note over User,LotterySvc: Phase 4: Lottery Draw (Admin)
    User->>+API: POST /events/{id}/draw
    API->>+LotterySvc: RunDraw(event_id)
    
    LotterySvc->>+PostgreSQL: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: tx started
    
    LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: SELECT title, status, winner_count,<br/>draw_at <= now()<br/>FROM events WHERE id=?<br/>FOR UPDATE (row lock)
    PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: status='closed', winner_count=1, due=true

    alt Status NOT 'closed'
        LotterySvc-->>API: ErrEventNotClosed / ErrEventAlreadyDrawn
        API-->>User: 409 Conflict
    end

    alt draw_at not yet reached
        LotterySvc-->>API: ErrDrawNotDue
        API-->>User: 409 draw_not_due
    end
    
    LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: SELECT user_id FROM bookings<br/>WHERE event_id=?<br/>ORDER BY booked_at
    PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: [user_1, user_2, ..., user_n]
    
    LotterySvc->>LotterySvc: crypto/rand Fisher-Yates shuffle<br/>SelectWinners(participants, winner_count)
    
    Note right of LotterySvc: Cryptographically<br/>secure randomness<br/>from kernel entropy
    
    loop For each winner (rank 1..winner_count)
        LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO lottery_draws<br/>(event_id, winner_user_id, draw_rank,<br/>entropy_source='crypto/rand+fisher-yates')
        PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: draw record created
    end
    
    loop For each waitlist (rank winner_count+1..n)
        LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO lottery_draws<br/>(event_id, winner_user_id, draw_rank)
        PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: draw record created
    end
    
    LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO lottery_draw_seals<br/>(event_id, SHA-256 digest of full ordered outcome)
    PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: seal stored (append-only)

    LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE events<br/>SET status='drawn'<br/>WHERE id=?
    PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: status updated

    LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: COMMIT
    PostgreSQL-->>-LotterySvc: committed (atomic)

    LotterySvc->>LotterySvc: Log digest at warn level<br/>(off-database copy)

    LotterySvc-->>-API: DrawResult{winners, waitlist, digest}
    API-->>-User: 200 OK with full results + digest

    Note over User,LotterySvc: Phase 5: View Results (Public)
    User->>+API: GET /events/{id}/results
    API->>+LotterySvc: GetResults(event_id)
    LotterySvc->>+PostgreSQL: SELECT * FROM lottery_draws<br/>WHERE event_id=?<br/>ORDER BY draw_rank
    PostgreSQL-->>LotterySvc: all draw records (append-only)
    LotterySvc->>PostgreSQL: SELECT digest FROM lottery_draw_seals
    PostgreSQL-->>-LotterySvc: stored seal
    LotterySvc->>LotterySvc: Recompute digest and compare
    LotterySvc-->>-API: DrawResult + integrity
    API-->>-User: 200 OK with integrity = verified or mismatch
